+> **Description:** PaddleOCR describes itself as a practical ultra-lightweight OCR system that supports text detection, recognition, document layout analysis, and multilingual scenarios. Its README makes clear that it covers far more than plain OCR, including structured parsing, table understanding, and PP-Structure pipelines for complex documents. Restaurants can apply it to printed menus, POS exports, supplier invoices, and onboarding documents that need to become searchable data. It is one of the strongest open source OCR options for production pipelines. On GitHub, PaddleOCR shows about 61k stars, Python as the primary language, an Apache-2.0 license, and recent GitHub activity through 2026-03-24.
