+#### [whisper.cpp](https://github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp)
+> **Description:** whisper.cpp is a high-performance C/C++ port of OpenAI's Whisper model focused on efficient speech-to-text inference on commodity hardware. The README emphasizes local execution, cross-platform support, quantization, and real-time or near-real-time transcription. For restaurants, that makes it attractive for voice-order capture, voicemail transcription, drive-thru experimentation, and call-center logging without sending audio to a closed vendor. It is an infrastructure component rather than a complete call product, but it is one of the most important open source pieces in the speech stack. On GitHub, whisper.cpp shows about 55k stars, C++ as the primary language, an MIT license, and recent GitHub activity through 2026-03-30.
+
