+## Why This List
+If you search for the best AI tools for restaurants in 2026, you quickly hit a market reality: most restaurant AI products are proprietary SaaS, while most genuinely open source options are adaptable infrastructure rather than restaurant-branded apps. This repository filters for public GitHub repositories only, excludes closed commercial tools, and groups the strongest self-hosted options by the restaurant jobs they can solve.
+
+That matters because restaurants need control over cost, data, integrations, and uptime. Open source tools let teams build voice ordering, menu parsing, internal copilots, forecasting, and recommendation workflows without locking guest data, recipes, or operating playbooks into a vendor black box.
