+## FAQ
+
+### What are the best open source AI tools for restaurants in 2026?
+For most teams, the best open source AI tools for restaurants in 2026 are not restaurant-branded apps. They are combinations of [Rasa](https://github.com/RasaHQ/rasa), [Dify](https://github.com/langgenius/dify), [PaddleOCR](https://github.com/PaddlePaddle/PaddleOCR), [whisper.cpp](https://github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp), [NeuralForecast](https://github.com/Nixtla/neuralforecast), and [Haystack](https://github.com/deepset-ai/haystack), depending on whether your priority is guest support, document extraction, voice, demand planning, or internal knowledge search.
+
+### Is there a fully open source AI ordering system for restaurants?
+Not really at the time of this research. That is the main gap in this market. There are open source components for speech, chat, retrieval, and workflow orchestration, but very few mature GitHub repositories that deliver a full restaurant ordering product end to end. Most teams will need to assemble a stack from several repos in this list.
+
+### Which open source AI tool is best for digitizing restaurant menus?
+[PaddleOCR](https://github.com/PaddlePaddle/PaddleOCR) is the strongest general choice, with [docTR](https://github.com/mindee/doctr), [Tesseract](https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tesseract), [Unstructured](https://github.com/Unstructured-IO/unstructured), and [Docling](https://github.com/ds4sd/docling) filling out the workflow from raw menu images to structured text and retrieval-ready documents.
+
+### Which open source AI stack is best for restaurant phone ordering or call transcription?
+A practical open stack is [whisper.cpp](https://github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp) or [faster-whisper](https://github.com/SYSTRAN/faster-whisper) for speech-to-text, [Piper](https://github.com/rhasspy/piper) or [TTS](https://github.com/coqui-ai/TTS) for speech output, and [Rasa](https://github.com/RasaHQ/rasa) or [Flowise](https://github.com/flowiseai/flowise) for conversation logic.
+
+### Which open source AI tools help restaurants forecast demand and reduce waste?
+[NeuralForecast](https://github.com/Nixtla/neuralforecast), [Darts](https://github.com/unit8co/darts), and [Prophet](https://github.com/facebook/prophet) are the most directly useful in this list for covers, sales, staffing, prep, and food-waste forecasting. [Microsoft Recommenders](https://github.com/microsoft/recommenders) and [RecBole](https://github.com/RUCAIBox/RecBole) are better for personalization and upsell ranking than pure demand planning.
+
+### Are there enough restaurant-specific GitHub repos to build a pure vertical awesome list?
+No. That is why this repository openly broadens scope to self-hosted AI tools that map cleanly to restaurant jobs. If a future category has fewer than 5 good public repos, that gap should be documented rather than padded with weak or irrelevant projects.
